  "subdivision_of_building": "Ground floor/part first floor -  Commercial unit\nsecond and third floors - Office space ",
  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "PLANNING PERMISSION AND ADVERTISEMENT CONSENT FOR A NEW SHOPFRONT AND THE DISPLAY OF INTERNALLY ILLUMINATED FASCIA SIGN AND INTERNALLY ILLUMINATED PROJECTING SIGN.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-bottom:0cm&quot;&gt;The proposal by reason of its combined siting and design fails to demonstrate\r\na design-led response to the site and would result in a shopfront and signage\r\nthat are visually intrusive and unsympathetic to the architectural character of\r\nthe locally listed building. The proposal fails to&amp;nbsp;&lt;span style=&quot;text-indent: -18pt;&quot;&gt;conserve or enhance the significance of the\r\nheritage asset,&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-indent: -18pt;&quot;&gt;introduces excessive and poorly integrated\r\nsignage and&lt;font face=&quot;Times New Roman&quot; size=&quot;1&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-indent: -18pt;&quot;&gt;does not respond positively to local character\r\nor context. The proposal is contrary to, in particular, p&lt;/span&gt;olicies D12.3, D12.4, D12.5 and D12.7, and the\r\nCouncil’s adopted Shopfront Design Guidance (2017).&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
